EPENDENT_REVIEW`. Organizational-independence credit 0 (Anthropic / Claude, the packets' author). Coordination: main#307 pickup [6136169673](https://github.com/d6g8k5htny-coder/main/issues/307#issuecomment-6136169673).\n\n**What it adds.** At the base `8acc4856` (current Math- main) the sibling proof packet proves 77 of the 141 registered Props. One new section, inserted identically into both documents before their closing sections, classifies the other 64 so the remaining formal work is named where the register lives:\n\n- **36 vocabulary predicates**: `def … : Prop` with explicit non-instance arguments, consumed only as hypotheses; the universal closure is false or empty, so they are not theorem targets (counted among the 141 because the register inventories every Prop-valued definition).\n- **24 interface-blocked**: the pinned interface's fields do not determine the conclusion; for each row the (mathematical, not kernel-checked) inhabitant that satisfies every field and violates the conclusion is named; the route is a numbered successor interface, not a cleverer proof.\n- **4 Mathlib-blocked**: Lifetime Theorems B, C, E11 and R1, whose truth value the interface fixes but whose proofs need Gaussian-field and density theory absent from Mathlib `d13f23b7`.\n\nSo of the 105 target Props, 77 are proved and 28 remain, all blocked at the specification or library level. Each row cites the defining line of the statement module (last changed at `873c6c0`, before the round-4 triage of 2026-10-11 whose verdicts this section re-applies). One cross-reference clause is added next to each document's existing \"77 of the 141 Props\" sentence.\n\n**Identities (head `9fb0a4a06900da5cc3f9126f30e117a747df1587`, tree `5f1ceda12195d71d178fcad1937dc2b57faa74ea`, base `8acc48566de3ae613c1ae320903b66c1d5411797`):**\n\n| file | bytes | blob | sha256 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `README.md` | 95031 | `756e3378` | `ff31f359e1ef514cd6dd2d6d45578b0c1d05b2984e3d759bc727dd1a01c19e3b` |\n| `SCOPE.md` | 273906 | `66b6a30a` | `762c0475dd4a5a28b5bd34a93d29616614b4b2e445ad4ab5feeff38e2f003693` |\n\n**Local checks on this head:** `python3 -B -S specifications/lean_statements_20261010/check.py` (source mode) exit 0, worktree CLEAN, 357 statements, 9 structures; `test_check.py` 97 tests OK. **Hosted runs on PR head `9fb0a4a0`, actual tested merge `6b6b53e817b98cd1ad2ddfb7df125125b17e96a3` (merge of `9fb0a4a0` into base `8acc4856`; `checked_commit` in both receipts):** `lean-specifications.yml` run 38333584611 (job 115088584979, success; artifact `lean-specifications-38333584611-1`, 42,022 B, sha256 `9c617f54f73f0684685c1f058039a68307b490eaf916f9345291631a856991fe`; register sha256 `bcafecbb…` unchanged) and `lean-specification-proofs.yml` run 38333584286 (job 115088583452, success; `theorem_count` 78, `leanchecker` PASS; artifact `lean-specification-proofs-38333584286-1`, 47,042 B, sha256 `0ecf5f4adece4a9016d3b86dc6451bed1064ce1aa13f063d132644c3244cf33a`); `downstream-replay`, `formal / formal-evidence` and `math-downstream-gates` also success: 5 of 5 check runs green on this head. These runs re-check the unchanged Lean packets; a green run on a docs-only change is a record of a computation, not evidence about the documents. Generator: a fail-closed exact-anchor script over the committed bytes (anchors asserted unique; the 64 names asserted equal to the register's def_props minus the proof packet's theorem types; counts 36 + 24 + 4 asserted), kept in the author's scratch and listed in the recovery checkpoint.\n\n**What this does not establish.** Nothing about the truth of any statement or claim. The classification is the author's single reading (this session's parallel-verification capacity is exhausted until 2026-10-17 03:00Z); a reader may move a row between classes, and the \"interface-blocked\" inhabitants are described, not formalised. It does not say the informal sources are wrong: their hypotheses are exactly what the interfaces do not transcribe. Nothing here i